        You will be given the root cause of a bug, the commit message and the corresponding patch.
        You need to extract all code statements that lead to the bug from the patch, based on the root cause and the commit message.

        Root cause:
        The bug was likely caused by the presence of the `gboolean style_append` variable in the `legacy_params` function, which may have interfered with the correct handling of legacy export presets, leading to issues when processing older parameter formats. Its removal across multiple image format files suggests it was not needed for the intended functionality and could have contributed to the malfunctioning of legacy parameter handling.

        Commit message:
        Fix broken legacy_params in some imageio formats

This fixes a bug introduced in 5f13d2527398eb82591fea828bbee7f13f1cc8f7
which most likely broke people's old export presets. Given how old it is
and the lack of complaints it's probably only a minor issue though. :-)  

        Patch:

 void *legacy_params(dt_imageio_module_format_t *self, const void *const old_params,
                     const size_t old_params_size, const int old_version, const int new_version,
                     size_t *new_size)
 {
   if(old_version == 1 && new_version == 2)
   {
     typedef struct dt_imageio_j2k_v1_t
     {
       int max_width, max_height;
       int width, height;
       char style[128];
-      gboolean style_append;
       int bpp;
       dt_imageio_j2k_format_t format;
       dt_imageio_j2k_preset_t preset;
       int quality;
     } dt_imageio_j2k_v1_t;

     dt_imageio_j2k_v1_t *o = (dt_imageio_j2k_v1_t *)old_params;
     dt_imageio_j2k_t *n = (dt_imageio_j2k_t *)malloc(sizeof(dt_imageio_j2k_t));

     n->max_width = o->max_width;
     n->max_height = o->max_height;
     n->width = o->width;
     n->height = o->height;
     g_strlcpy(n->style, o->style, sizeof(o->style));
     n->style_append = 0;
     n->bpp = o->bpp;
     n->format = o->format;
     n->preset = o->preset;
     n->quality = o->quality;
     *new_size = self->params_size(self);
     return n;
   }
   return NULL;
 }



